00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:19.280
Machine learning is an
incredibly useful approach

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.290
to automating tasks with data.

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:24.550
But how do you bring it to
multi-cloud hybrid environments

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:26.310
as an entire stack?

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:28.476
Applying it is about more
than just the algorithms.

00:00:28.476 --> 00:00:30.350
It's also about the
infrastructure, the data,

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.420
and all the other components.

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:34.550
You want your machine
learning to be composable,

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:37.310
so it accommodates all the
data science tools out there.

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:39.050
You want portability,
so it's easy to go

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:41.210
from prototyping
models on your laptop

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:44.030
to running them
unchanged in production.

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:45.680
You want it to
scale effortlessly

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.744
from your small data prototype
to your huge data pipelines.

00:00:49.744 --> 00:00:52.160
You know what's really good
at composability, portability,

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:53.480
and scalability?

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:54.920
Containers and Kubernetes.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.470
Except if a data
scientist who wants to use

00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:58.970
machine learning on Kubernetes.

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:01.970
There's so many things that
have to be an expert in first.

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:03.740
They need a second
black belt in addition

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:05.260
to their machine learning one.

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:07.880
Enter Kubeflow, the
cloud-native machine

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:09.770
learning platform built
on Kubernetes to take

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:10.940
care of the entire stack.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:13.220
Kubeflow's mission is to
make it easy for everyone

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:15.620
to develop, deploy, and
manage portable distributed

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.450
machine learning on Kubernetes.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:20.966
And that means everyone, no
extra black belts needed.

00:01:20.966 --> 00:01:22.340
Kubeflow gives
you the components

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:24.830
you need for machine learning
right out of the box--

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:27.740
Jupyter notebooks, distributed
training, model serving,

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:30.860
examples, plus customizable
case net packaging

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:32.750
that lets you add your own.

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:35.580
But what about the data?

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:38.510
App portability needs
data portability.

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:40.700
Well, that's what
Elastifile's for.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.880
It gives you one-click setup and
straightforward sync strategies

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:46.070
all without having to
rewrite your applications.

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:49.400
If your app can use POSIX, NFS,
or standard block object store,

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:50.950
you can use Elastifile.

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:52.700
So Elastifile plus
Kubeflow means

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:55.490
you have everything you need
for truly portable machine

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:56.870
learning.

00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:58.970
There is a mountain
of things to take care

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:00.830
of if you do it on your own.

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:02.554
Why not take the
ski lift instead?

00:02:02.554 --> 00:02:04.470
In the full talk, you'll
see demos of Kubeflow

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:05.720
and Elastifile in action.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:07.760
And what's that I'm seeing here?

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:11.360
You can deploy Kubeflow with
a one-step script included

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:14.180
in the download, and that's
thanks to Kubeflow 0.2,

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:15.500
which we've just announced.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:17.390
The latest version
gives you added bonuses

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:20.360
like advanced tooling,
including H2O as a platform,

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:22.160
and really powerful
hyperparameter

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:23.630
tuning with Katib.

00:02:23.630 --> 00:02:25.600
We also have platform
integrations including

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:27.550
autoscaling based
on job submission,

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:30.080
cloud-specific
accelerators and VMs,

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.810
and data exfiltration
prevention.

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:36.770
Data science is poised to
revolutionize every industry,

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:38.810
and Kubeflow is helping
by giving everyone

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:41.900
a single environment to do
reproducible, production-ready

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:44.270
machine learning without
having to know all the gory

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:46.130
behind the scenes details.

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:48.902
And the momentum is incredible.

